OUTER_SPRINT bard_song_description ~The Bard can sing at will. A song lasts six rounds, plus one round for every five Bard levels. After activating a song, the Bard must wait one turn to sing again. The standard song protects allies from fear and morale failure, and grants +1 Luck. Luck rises to +2 at level 15 and +3 at level 20.~
ACTION_IF GAME_IS ~iwdee~ BEGIN
  OUTER_SPRINT bard_song_description ~The Bard can perform the following songs while the Bard Song modal is active.
Level 1, Ballad of Three Heroes: Allies gain +1 to hit, damage and saving throws.
Level 3, Tale of Curran Strongheart: Allies gain immunity to fear, and existing fear is removed.
Level 5, Tymora's Melody: Allies gain +1 Luck, +3 to saving throws, +10 Lore and +10% to thieving skills.
Level 7, Song of Kaudies: Allies have a 50% chance to shrug off sound-based attacks.
Level 9, Siren's Yearning: Enemies must save vs. Spell or become enthralled for one round. Damage ends the enthrallment.
Level 11, War Chant of Sith: Allies gain +2 Armor Class, 10% resistance to physical damage and regenerate 2 Hit Points per round.~
END

OUTER_SPRINT bard_armor_casting ~(Spells cannot be cast while wearing armor.)~
ACTION_IF MOD_IS_INSTALLED ~BardicWonders/Setup-BardicWonders.tp2~ ~2003~ BEGIN
  OUTER_SPRINT bard_armor_casting ~(Spells may be cast while wearing up to studded leather armor.)~
END

OUTER_SPRINT bard_description ~BARD: A wandering musician and storyteller, the Bard uses charm, lore, arcane magic and song to support the party.

Class features:
– May not wear armor heavier than chain mail. %bard_armor_casting%
– May not equip shields larger than bucklers.
– Can become Proficient (one slot) in weapon and fighting-style proficiencies.
– Can Pick Pockets and gains an increased Lore score.
– Gains arcane spellcasting at 2nd level.
– Alignment restricted to any neutral.
– Hit Die: d6.

Bard Song
%bard_song_description%~

ACTION_IF FILE_EXISTS_IN_GAME ~CLASTEXT.2DA~ BEGIN
  COPY_EXISTING ~CLASTEXT.2DA~ ~override~
    COUNT_2DA_COLS columns
    READ_2DA_ENTRIES_NOW classes columns
    FOR (row = 0; row < classes; ++row) BEGIN
      READ_2DA_ENTRY_FORMER classes row 0 class_name
      PATCH_IF ~%class_name%~ STRING_EQUAL_CASE ~BARD~ BEGIN
        SET_2DA_ENTRY row 4 columns RESOLVE_STR_REF (~%bard_description%~)
      END
    END
    PRETTY_PRINT_2DA
  BUT_ONLY
END
